.TH "CSSNUMERICVALUE.TOSUM" "3JS" "August 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSNumericValue.toSum \- CSSNumericValue: toSum() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]toSum()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] interface converts the object\(cqs value to a
\f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R] of \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R]s using only the
specified units, if possible.
If called with no units, it simplifies the value into a minimal sum of
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R]s instead.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toSum()
toSum(unit1)
toSum(unit1, unit2)
toSum(unit1, unit2, /* \&..., */ unitN)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]unit1\f[R], \&..., \f[B]unitN\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
The units to convert to.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]CSSMathSum\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]SyntaxError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if any of \f[CR]unit1\f[R], \&..., \f[CR]unitN\f[R] is not a
valid unit identifier.
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
The value can\(cqt be expressed as a sum of \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R]s
\(em for example, because one of its terms has a compound unit (such as
\f[CR]px * s\f[R]) that can\(cqt be represented by a single
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
One or more units were passed to the method, and the value includes a
term whose unit isn\(cqt compatible with any of them.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
.IP
.EX
\f[B]let\f[R] v = CSS.px(\(dq23\(dq).add(CSS.percent(\(dq4\(dq)).add(CSS.cm(\(dq3\(dq)).add(CSS.in(\(dq9\(dq));
v.toString(); \f[I]// => \(dqcalc(23px + 4% + 3cm + 9in)\(dq\f[R]
v.toSum(\(dqpx\(dq, \(dqpercent\(dq).toString(); \f[I]// => \(dqcalc(1000.39px + 4%)\(dq\f[R]
.EE
